  "observations": [
    "PGO remains mixed: the two use-mode win arms are 2.170001-2.180000 ms and 2.410001-2.420000 ms; their ordinary partners are 2.270001-2.280000 ms and 2.230001-2.240000 ms. No repeat of unchanged PGO is justified. Per-source means are not per-source p95s and cannot be subtracted from whole-tick p95.",
    "Current stress.ts still hashes to the original 7285e9009633052ba86ee0996c87f58097eb47fdaf0a73df10f42597b0119f1a and performs all 9,999-row writes/checksum reads. Loan foreign views point at ECS storage; undo capture is a separate required native copy with reused capacity, not duplicate guest transfer.",
    "Pinned QuickJS OP_get_array_el already uses js_get_fast_array_element for integer-index typed reads; its Float64Array case directly reads the double pointer. A generic typed-read optimization is not a new missing fast path. Typed-store/loop patches were already measured negative or mixed.",
    "Possible repeated character-query snapshot construction is not supported on the ordinary stepped route: NativeSession::tick_with_ui steps the world before ScriptHost, PhysicsRuntime::step clears query_dirty, and character_motion borrows query_pipeline_with_filter when clean. The dirty-author-edit fallback is distinct; no evidence shows it dominating the current Core route.",
    "with_numeric_physics moves the solver/navigation owners rather than cloning them; NativeLocalization clones Arcs, and spatial_view only checks usability/borrows the world. These are not hidden whole-world/catalog copies to eliminate.",
    "Historical full-Core instrumented tail attribution places 78.19% of the same 108 tail frames inside inclusive callbacks. Numeric validation averages 195.481 us on those frames; ordered-query and matrix-basis changes have already failed matched adoption. The existing evidence does not separate callback interpreter work from individual native query/serialization cost.",
    "Historical same-frame subtraction of all navigation still reranks to 2.171792 ms. Deadline checks average 4.34 us overall and 8.40 us on the retained tail. Neither repeating navigation-only work nor weakening deadline enforcement has a supported path to the unmet target."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Do not open another speculative optimization branch or repeat the rejected experiments from this revisit. The next useful trigger is new source-bound attribution of a distinct callback subpath on the unchanged current Core route; until then the 2 ms gate remains unmet and no saving is predicted.",
  "conditional_measurement_design": {
    "status": "not authorized, not implemented, not a claimed optimization candidate",
    "purpose": "If a future CPU lane is allocated, distinguish QuickJS interpreter property/number/dispatch cost from native capability parse/execute/materialize cost before proposing a change. Retain current source/guest binaries and do not infer duration from PGO execution counts.",
    "baseline_contract": "Use the ordinary source-free shipping recipe, exact C compiler/options, Rust opt3/fat-LTO/one-CGU/abort, actual closed physics feature graph, identical profile observer, original 74 authoring inputs and full 2,156-tick route. Treat any instrumented/sampled child as diagnostic only.",
    "falsification_and_parity": "Require exact all-tick gameplay observations and complete 13,798,400-byte win PCM against the same-source ordinary control; retain failure/partial data. Include held-out loss and restart parity for any later implementation. A hypothesized hotspot must show a meaningful attributed cost in the same slow frames; counts or inclusive callback totals alone are insufficient.",
    "later_matched_change_only_if_supported": "Freeze one small cause-specific implementation, run complete functional/PCM parity before a fixed balanced quiet shipping comparison, keep all samples and pair results, and report PlayerFrame/memory separately. No threshold adjustment, no pooled quantiles, no guarantee of 2 ms."
  },
